Fix the CONSYS shared-DRAM reservation to the stock Biscuit address

The original mainline port allocates a two-megabyte `consys-pool` dynamically
below 512 MiB.  On Device #1 that produced `0x5f400000` and consequently
programmed CONSYS_EMI_MAPPING as `0x11f4`.  The successful instrumented
FireOS kernel on the otherwise-identical Device #3 instead reserves
`0x5f600000..0x5f7fffff` and programs `0x11f6`.

That physical window is part of the firmware ABI: the connectivity processor
uses it for WMT/STP shared state and coredump buffers.  A valid chip ID and a
working TX DMA ring do not prove that a different window is usable.  Make the
reservation exact so the generic driver computes the stock mapping and its
existing region-13 MPU setup from the correct base.

This intentionally does not change the rail sequence, reset release timing,
BTIF DMA setup, or the native STP/WMT implementation.  It supersedes the
unverified CONNMCU clock experiment that previously occupied patch number
0075.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8163-amazon-biscuit.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8163-amazon-biscuit.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8163-amazon-biscuit.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8163-amazon-biscuit.dts
@@ -723,3 +723,15 @@
 &consys {
	mediatek,emi = <&emi>;
 };
+
+/*
+ * FireOS on Biscuit reserves this exact 2 MiB ABI window.  Do not let the
+ * early allocator choose a different aligned location: CONSYS firmware sees
+ * the address encoded in infracfg's CONSYS_EMI_MAPPING register.
+ */
+&consys_mem {
+	reg = <0x0 0x5f600000 0x0 0x00200000>;
+	/delete-property/ size;
+	/delete-property/ alignment;
+	/delete-property/ alloc-ranges;
+};
